-- title:
--   Conjugation by a finite idèle preserves intersections and inclusions
-- statement:
--   Let $a,b\in\mathbb{Q}$ and let $\Lambda,\Lambda'$ be $\mathbb{Z}$-submodules of the quaternion algebra $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$, each an order in the sense of the predicate `IsOrder`: it contains $1$, is closed under multiplication, its $\mathbb{Q}$-span is all of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$, and it is finitely generated over $\mathbb{Z}$. Let $g$ be a unit of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q},f}$, where $\mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q},f}$ is the finite adèle ring of $\mathbb{Q}$. For a $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule $\Lambda$, [`Submodule.finiteAdeleBox`](def/Submodule_FiniteAdeleBox.html#L14) $\Lambda$ is the additive subgroup of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q},f}$ generated by the elements $z\otimes c$ with $z\in\Lambda$ and $c$ a finite adèle whose component at every height-one prime $v$ of $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$ lies in the ring of integers of the $v$-adic completion, and [`Submodule.conjByFiniteIdele`](def/Submodule_FiniteAdeleBox.html#L31) $\Lambda\,g$ is the $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ consisting of those $z$ with $z\otimes 1$ in the image of that box under $x\mapsto gxg^{-1}$. The theorem asserts two things: first, $\mathrm{conj}(\Lambda\sqcap\Lambda',g)=\mathrm{conj}(\Lambda,g)\sqcap\mathrm{conj}(\Lambda',g)$; second, if $\Lambda\le\Lambda'$ then $\mathrm{conj}(\Lambda,g)\le\mathrm{conj}(\Lambda',g)$.
--
--   This is the compatibility of the adelic conjugation operation on lattices with the lattice operations of intersection and inclusion, part of the local–global dictionary for orders in a rational quaternion algebra. It is used in the construction of fake elliptic curves with prescribed endomorphism order in the Čerednik–Drinfel'd part of the development.
